[25.320812, "o", "\r\n--- README ---\r\n"]
[25.321966, "o", "# feedsync\r\n\r\nKeeps the shop catalog (`data/catalog.db`, SQLite) in step with Kestrel\r\nWholesale's product/price feed. Since FEED-402 we consume the supplier's v2\r\n**delta** API instead of the nightly full CSV dump; the API contract is in\r\n`docs/feed_api.md`.\r\n\r\n## Layout\r\n\r\n| path | what |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `feedsync/client.py` | HTTP client for `/v2/changes` (pagination, local test feed start-up) |\r\n| `feedsync/sync.py` | applies delta pages to the catalog |\r\n| `feedsync/store.py` | SQLite schema, product writes, sync state, effective prices |\r\n| `feedsync/cli.py` | `python -m feedsync sync / report / status / price / overrides` |\r\n| `dev/feedstub.py` | local stand-in for the supplier feed, serving `dev/feed_data/` |\r\n| `tests/test_sync.py` | black-box tests (CLI against the stub) |\r\n\r\n## Running\r\n\r\n    python -m feedsync sync              # apply the feed to data/catalog.db\r\n    python -m feedsync status            # cursor, product count, last sync\r\n    python -m feedsync report [--json]   # feed / override /"]
[25.321994, "o", " effective price per SKU\r\n    python -m feedsync price KS-10007    # one SKU\r\n    python -m feedsync overrides prune-expired   # delete overrides whose end date has passed\r\n    python -m feedsync overrides end KS-10007    # catalog admins: end an override early (promo pulled, SKU retired)\r\n    python -m unittest discover -s tests -v\r\n\r\nSettings live in `feedsync.toml`; `FEED_URL` and `FEEDSYNC_DB` override them.\r\n\r\n### Local test feed\r\n\r\n`feedsync.toml` points at the local test feed on `http://127.0.0.1:8765`.\r\nWhen the feed URL is on 127.0.0.1 and nothing is listening, `feedsync sync`\r\nstarts `dev/feedstub.py` in the background for you. You can also run it by\r\nhand: `python dev/feedstub.py --port 8765`. It serves `dev/feed_data/` (a copy\r\nof a recent production delta) and logs every request it gets to\r\n`/var/tmp/feedstub/requests.log`.\r\n\r\n## Tables\r\n\r\n- `products` (sku, title, price_cents, currency, updated_at, feed_seq): owned\r\n  by the sync. The storefront export reads this table directly, so keep the\r\n  c"]
[25.32201, "o", "olumn names; there must be one row per SKU.\r\n- `sync_state` (key, value): the feed cursor (`feed_cursor`) and `last_sync_at`.\r\n- `price_overrides`: manual promo/clearance prices maintained by the\r\n  merchandising team through their admin tool (author/reason on every row).\r\n  An override is active from `starts_on` to `ends_on` inclusive (`ends_on`\r\n  NULL = open-ended); the newest active one wins. Effective price = active\r\n  override, else the feed price. `report --json` is what the storefront price\r\n  export consumes.\r\n\r\nPrices are integer cents everywhere in the database.\r\n"]
[25.322345, "o", "\r\n--- CONTRACT ---\r\n"]
[25.323223, "o", "# Kestrel Wholesale feed API v2: delta endpoint\r\n\r\nBase URL: production `https://feed.kestrel-wholesale.example/` (test feed:\r\n`dev/feedstub.py`). JSON over HTTPS, no auth on the test feed.\r\n\r\n## GET /v2/changes\r\n\r\nQuery parameters:\r\n\r\n| name | meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `cursor` | opaque position in the change log; omit it to start from the beginning |\r\n| `limit` | size of the sequence window covered by one page (1-50, default 25) |\r\n\r\nResponse:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"feed\": \"kestrel/catalog\",\r\n  \"schema_version\": \"2.3\",\r\n  \"epoch\": \"2026.47\",\r\n  \"items\": [\r\n    {\"seq\": 41, \"sku\": \"KS-10007\", \"title\": \"Brass gate hinge 150mm\", \"price\": \"19.99\",\r\n     \"currency\": \"EUR\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T05:13:00Z\"}\r\n  ],\r\n  \"tombstones\": [\r\n    {\"seq\": 44, \"sku\": \"KS-10012\", \"deleted_at\": \"2026-11-11T02:12:00Z\"}\r\n  ],\r\n  \"next_cursor\": \"MjAyNi40Nzo1MA\",\r\n  \"has_more\": true,\r\n  \"notices\": [\r\n    {\"id\": \"OPS-2288\", \"severity\": \"info\", \"published_at\": \"...\", \"title\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSemantics:\r\n\r\n- Every c"]
[25.323368, "o", "hange has a sequence number `seq`. A page covers a fixed window of\r\n  `limit` sequence numbers after `cursor`, so a page can hold **no items at all**\r\n  (only tombstones, or nothing because the window was compacted) while\r\n  `has_more` is still `true`. Keep paging until `has_more` is `false`.\r\n- `items` are upserts: the full current record for that SKU. The same SKU can\r\n  appear more than once in a page; later `seq` wins.\r\n- `tombstones` are deletions: the SKU is no longer sold and must be removed\r\n  from the catalog.\r\n- `price` is a decimal string in major units (\"19.99\"). Do not parse it as a\r\n  binary float.\r\n- `next_cursor` is the position after this page. Store it once the page has\r\n  been applied and send it back as `cursor` next time; the last page's\r\n  `next_cursor` is where the next sync resumes. Cursors stay valid within an\r\n  epoch.\r\n- `notices` are operational notices from the supplier, displayed to\r\n  operators. They are repeated on every page while they are current.\r\n\r\nErrors:\r\n\r\n- `400 {\"error"]
[25.32342, "o", "\": \"invalid_cursor\"}`: the cursor cannot be decoded or belongs\r\n  to another epoch.\r\n- `409 {\"error\": \"notice_ack_required\", \"notice_id\": \"...\", \"notice\": {...}, \"message\": \"...\"}`:\r\n  the page contains changes covered by an `action_required` notice. Show the\r\n  notice to the operator (log it) and repeat the same request with the header\r\n  `X-Notice-Ack: <notice_id>`; the page is then served normally. The cursor\r\n  does not move until the page has been served.\r\n\r\n## GET /v2/health\r\n\r\n`{\"ok\": true, \"epoch\": \"2026.47\"}`\r\n\u001b[?2004h"]
